    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4039\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to sales and compensating use\ntax in Dutchess county\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo extend until November 30, 2011 Dutchess County's authorization to\namend local laws, ordinances or resolutions in order to charge an\nadditional three-quarters of one percent sales and compensating use\ntax.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection one authorizes Dutchess County to extend the expiration date\nof its existing authorization to amend local laws, ordinances or\nresolutions to charge an additional three-quarters of once percent\nsales tax from November 30, 2009 to November 30, 2011.\n\nSection two provides this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nCurrent law will expire November 30, 2009.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Dutchess County Legislature has requested that legislation be\nintroduced in the State Legislature to extend the authorization for a\nlocal law to meet local fiscal considerations.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nChapter 528, Laws of 2007\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nIncreased local revenue is anticipated.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
